e1$ and $q'=e^{2\pi iw}
e1$; cross-multiplying, $qq'-q+q'-1=q'q-q'+q-1$, hence $2q'=2q$, $q=q'$, and $z-w\in\mathbb Z$ by [F9]. Thus $P$ is injective on the coset space $(\mathbb C\setminus\mathbb Z)/\mathbb Z$; since $P'
e0$ there by step 1.4, $P$ is locally biholomorphic on $\mathbb C\setminus\mathbb Z$.
